## Infrastructure Creation
kubectl config set-context --current --namespace=carshop

### Step 1 — Create a GKE Cluster
Create a GKE cluster where Prometheus and Grafana will be deployed.

### Step 2 — Create a Monitoring Namespace
Create a dedicated `monitor` namespace as a good Kubernetes practice - kubectl create namespace monitor

Step 3 — Access the Prometheus & Grafana Helm Chart - The Helm chart for Prometheus and Grafana is available in the Prometheus 
Community repository:
[kube-prometheus-stack Helm Chart]
(https://github.com/prometheus-community/helm-charts/tree/main/charts/kube-prometheus-stack?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

Step 4 — Add the Helm Repository
Add the Prometheus Community Helm repository and update the local Helm repository information.
helm repo add prometheus-community https://prometheus-community.github.io/helm-charts
helm repo update

Step 5 — Install Prometheus & Grafana - Install the `kube-prometheus-stack` Helm chart into the `monitor` namespace.
helm install kube-prometheus-stack prometheus-community/kube-prometheus-stack --namespace monitor

Notes - 
* **`kube-prometheus-stack`** → Name of the Helm release.
* **`prometheus-community/kube-prometheus-stack`** → Helm chart being installed.
* **`--namespace monitor`** → Deploys the monitoring stack into the `monitor` namespace.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Monitoring order -

1. Carshop Pod CPU Usage
query - sum by (pod) (
  rate(container_cpu_usage_seconds_total{
    namespace="carshop",
    container!="",
    container!="POD"
  }[5m])
)
---------------------------------------------------
2. Carshop Pod Memory Usage
sum by (pod) (
  container_memory_working_set_bytes{
    namespace="carshop",
    container!="",
    container!="POD"
  }
)
----------------------------------------------------
3. Pod Restarts (display pod in mb)
sum by (pod) (
  container_memory_working_set_bytes{
    namespace="carshop",
    container!="",
    container!="POD"
  }
) / 1024 / 1024
------------------------------------------------------
4. Running Pods
count(
  kube_pod_status_phase{
    namespace="carshop",
    phase="Running"
  } == 1
)
-------------------------------------------------------
5. Pending Pods
count(
  kube_pod_status_phase{
    namespace="carshop",
    phase="Pending"
  } == 1
)
--------------------------------------------------------
6. CPU Usage by Node
sum by (node) (
  rate(container_cpu_usage_seconds_total{
    container!="",
    container!="POD"
  }[5m])
)
----------------------------------------------------------
7. Memory Usage by Node
sum by (node) (
  container_memory_working_set_bytes{
    container!="",
    container!="POD"
  }
) / 1024 / 1024 / 1024
--------------------------------------------------------------
8. Network Traffic 
receive traffic -
sum by (pod) (
  rate(container_network_receive_bytes_total{
    namespace="carshop",
    pod!=""
  }[5m])
)
------------------------------
send traffic -
sum by (pod) (
  rate(container_network_transmit_bytes_total{
    namespace="carshop",
    pod!=""
  }[5m])
)
---------------------------------------------------------------
9. Pod Count
count(
  kube_pod_info{
    namespace="carshop"
  }
)
------------------------------------------------------------------
10. Application Request Rate
sum(
  rate(http_requests_total{
    namespace="carshop"
  }[5m])
)
